# Property Screener — Documentation Rules

> **Repository state**
>
> - **Committed baseline (`15b2c83`):** `portal.py`, analyze-only. No Compare or multi-page UI files.
> - **Local working tree (uncommitted):** `streamlit_app.py`, `app_pages/`, Compare, supporting modules; `portal.py` deleted locally.
> - **Never assume the refactor exists on a clean clone of `15b2c83`.** Run `git status` and inspect files when ambiguous.
> - **Streamlit UI:** **CURRENT** in the local tree; **TEMPORARY BRIDGE** architecturally (future target is a web app). Use both labels.

## Bootstrap

1. Read `docs/ai-context.md` first in a new or recovered session.
2. Read `docs/current-status.md` before handoff work or migration tasks.
3. Treat **repository code** as authoritative when docs conflict — then update docs.

## Repository state when documenting

- Distinguish **committed baseline** (`15b2c83`) from **local uncommitted** changes when behavior or availability matters.
- Run `git status` and confirm which files exist before stating what the repo supports.
- Never document an uncommitted feature (e.g. Compare, `streamlit_app.py`) as available on a clean checkout of `15b2c83`.

## Classification labels

Use these consistently in docs and comments:

| Label | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **CURRENT** | Implemented and in use **in the tree you are working in** (check git status) |
| **LEGACY** | Superseded; may still exist at older commits (e.g. `portal.py` at `15b2c83`) |
| **MIGRATION IN PROGRESS** | Partially done; especially uncommitted UI refactor |
| **ALREADY MIGRATED** | Done beyond original plan (e.g. Compare dashboard) |
| **TEMPORARY BRIDGE** | Works now but not long-term architecture — includes Streamlit UI (local) and Google Sheets |
| **FUTURE TARGET** | Planned; **not implemented** — never describe as existing |

## Source-of-truth hierarchy

1. Code (`scripts/`, `app_pages/`, `streamlit_app.py`)
2. `strategy.md` — investment weights, criteria, philosophy
3. `scripts/write_to_sheets.py` `HEADERS` — Sheet schema
4. `prompts/` + `schema/` — AI contracts
5. `docs/` — synthesized context (update when 1–4 change meaningfully)

Do **not** duplicate full strategy content outside `strategy.md`.

## Entry points

- **Local working tree:** `streamlit_app.py` + `app_pages/` (**CURRENT** / **TEMPORARY BRIDGE**)
- **Committed baseline (`15b2c83`):** `portal.py` (analyze-only)
- **LEGACY** (relative to local refactor): `portal.py` — deleted locally, present at `15b2c83`

## Future architecture guardrails

- No REST API, auth, production DB, or cloud deployment exists today.
- Framer Motion belongs to the **FUTURE TARGET** React/Next.js-style frontend — not Streamlit.
- Do not lock frontend/backend stack unless the repo establishes it.
- Google Sheets is the **CURRENT** store and **TEMPORARY BRIDGE** — not already replaced.
- Manual listing paste is **CURRENT** v1 ingestion — no scraping unless explicitly built.
- Weighted overall score is computed in `scoring.py` — the LLM does not set it.

## When to update documentation

Update docs after **meaningful** changes — not for trivial one-line bug fixes.

| Change type | Primary docs to review/update |
|-------------|-------------------------------|
| Schema / data / Sheet columns | `database-schema.md`, `architecture.md`, `current-status.md` |
| Product behavior / workflows | `product-requirements.md`, `current-status.md` |
| Architecture / modules / integrations | `architecture.md`, `ai-context.md`, `project-decisions.md` |
| Investment strategy / weights | `strategy.md` (canonical), `investment-criteria.md` (implementation only) |
| Deployment / env / config | `architecture.md`, `current-status.md`, `README.md` |
| Migration / web app planning | `web-migration.md`, `roadmap.md` |
| Legacy removal | `current-status.md`, `project-decisions.md`, `web-migration.md` |
| Important project context | `ai-context.md`, `current-status.md` |
| Ordinary bug fix | Usually none — avoid documentation churn |

## Legacy removal

- **Verify migration completion in code** before removing legacy systems.
- Never delete `portal.py`, Sheets integration, or Streamlit files solely because docs say they are planned for removal.
- Document the removal in `current-status.md` and `project-decisions.md` after it happens.

## Security

- Never copy secrets, API keys, tokens, or credential file contents into docs.
- Do not commit `.env`, `credentials/`, or `keys ect....odt`.
- Do not open or summarize sensitive untracked files unless absolutely necessary.

## After context summarization

Recover by reading `docs/ai-context.md`, `docs/current-status.md`, and inspecting git status — not by assuming prior conversation state.

## Conciseness

Keep docs short and useful. Prefer updating existing files over creating new ones. No documentation bureaucracy.
